# Homelab — Docker only

On **homelab** (`~/doorface`), Doorface runs **entirely in Docker**. Do not add or document
host-level app setup outside that boundary.

**Deploy shape:** Mac `rsync worker/` → `~/doorface`, then remote `docker compose build/up`.
Secrets in `~/doorface/.env` only (never rsync'd; created from `.env.example` on first deploy).
Host installs **platform only** (NVIDIA driver, Docker, Container Toolkit) — not app Python.

**Bind-mounted `config/`:** use `DOCKER_UID` / `DOCKER_GID` in `.env` so web enroll writes faces
and gallery with permissions the container user can write. Fix old root-owned files via
`scripts/fix-homelab-config-perms.sh` (container `chown`, not host `sudo`).

## Do

- `bun run deploy` from Mac (rsync code + `docker compose build/up` on homelab)
- `docker compose up|build|logs|ps` in `~/doorface`
- One-off GPU tasks via `docker compose run` or `docker run --gpus all` with the worker image
- Secrets and tuning in `~/doorface/.env` (never rsync'd from Mac)
- Fix file ownership on mounted `config/` **via a container** (e.g. `docker compose run … chown`)
  when needed — not `sudo chown` on the host

## Do not

- Install Python, venv, `pip install -r requirements-vision.txt`, or apt packages on the homelab
  **host** for Doorface
- Run `enroll.py` / `main.py` with homelab host `python3.11` or `~/doorface/.venv`
- Suggest `ssh homelab 'sudo chown …'` or other host mutations outside Docker
- Add systemd units, cron, or bare-metal services for the worker — use `compose.yaml`

## Mac vs homelab

| Task                       | Mac          | Homelab     |
| -------------------------- | ------------ | ----------- |
| Edit, pytest, lint         | ✓            | —           |
| InsightFace / GPU          | —            | Docker only |
| Enrollment photos          | —            | web UI (`/enroll`) |
| Prod worker (`/recognize`) | —            | Docker only |
